+# Current physical case-alias support repair
+
+2026-10-16T04:20:14.191765+00:00
+
+CASE-1071 is a new P3 output-location finding after two completed whole reviews (minimum two); historical whole02 had zero actionable findings. The shared fresh_output preflight now checks the physical identity of every existing output ancestor against the frozen root, including ancestors above absent intermediate directories and both case-spelling directions. It preserves absent destinations, existing real parents, lexical and resolved containment, no symlink ancestors, existing hardlink rejection and the new-empty-directory boundary for checker/compiler child files. Parent traversal components are rejected before normalization so a symlink cannot be hidden by lexical collapse. No case-folding heuristic is used. This remains a static local preflight without concurrent mutation guarantees.
+
+CASE_ALIAS_REPAIR_STATUS.json is the current workflow record: pending NEW complete whole03 and root repair/terminal adoption; publication_ready, issues_resolved and published false; ordered services held after PR1032. Earlier STATUS/CURRENT_STATUS/TERMINAL_STATUS/FINAL_ACCEPTANCE and external ROOT seals retain their exact historical bytes. The new program support hold supersedes former readiness. This bounded repair is not whole03 or publication approval.
+
+The theorem, seven-page paper PDF/source, all native bibliographic metadata objects, original finite checker, citation and source credits remain unchanged. The all-H, all-T, all-n, both-grid, every-L2-estimator statement and its exclusions are those of the accepted paper. Brownian optimum and smooth rate are prior, Fourier/Gaussian antecedents are credited, full priority/novelty/open status UNKNOWN; no journal-error, firstness, human review or formal certification claim is added. No new actual paper compile, render or PDF marker is required or claimed here: unchanged whole02 already compiled both modes and viewed all seven pages.
+
+The first 116 copy rows remain exact and ordered. New exact safe interface history and old root readiness/terminal evidence are appended; CASE_ALIAS_SOURCE_EVIDENCE.json is explicitly a scoped authored excerpt with full source pins. Every omitted prior ZIP/sidecar or unselected terminal/scope file is individually hash-accounted for. No third-party full source, extract, image, runtime or raw stream is added; no omitted historical program is claimed replayed. The external publication/zenodo-deposit.json stays native and byte-exact; included deposit.json remains a historical metadata wrapper.
